        <body>
            <div xml:id="d18-a1">

                <pb facs="0384" n="374" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv09/pg374"/>

                <head>Appendix A to HD–102</head>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">Surrendered Enemy Submarines</hi></p>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Summary of Situation</hi>, 28<hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">th November</hi>, 1919</p>
                <p>1. At a meeting of the Admirals on 27th June 1919, all except the French were in
                    favor of the destruction of all surrendered enemy submarines.</p>
                <p>2. After the surrender of the submarines, it was agreed that a certain number
                    should be broken up, but when fifty-four had been sold for breaking up, it was
                    agreed by the Supreme Council that no more should be broken up pending a
                    decision on the whole question of the disposal of the enemy fleets. The proceeds
                    of the fifty-four which have been broken up are being held in trust for the
                    Allies in the same way as the submarines themselves.</p>
                <p>3. A certain number of submarines have been supplied to France, Italy, U. S. A.,
                    Japan and Belgium for propaganda purposes, viz. <table cols="2"
                        rend="width: 50%;" rendition="#center" rows="6">
                        <row role="label">
                            <cell>Great Britain</cell>
                            <cell role="num">5</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell>France</cell>
                            <cell role="num">15</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell>Italy</cell>
                            <cell role="num">10</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell>U. S. A.</cell>
                            <cell role="num">6</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell>Japan</cell>
                            <cell rendition="#underline" role="num">7</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell rendition="#float-right">Total</cell>
                            <cell role="num">43</cell>
                        </row>
                    </table></p>
                <p rendition="#flush">and Belgium has been loaned one for a few weeks.</p>
                <p>4. The present situation of enemy submarines including those for propaganda
                    purposes is as follows: <table cols="2" rend="width: 70%;" rendition="#center"
                        rows="7">
                        <row role="label">
                            <cell><hi rendition="#italic">Country</hi></cell>
                            <cell><hi rendition="#italic">Number</hi></cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell>Great Britain (49, and 54 sold for breaking up)</cell>
                            <cell role="num">103</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell>France</cell>
                            <cell role="num">46</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell>Italy (18 completed Austrian and 10 German)</cell>
                            <cell role="num">28</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell>U. S. A.</cell>
                            <cell role="num">6</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell>Japan</cell>
                            <cell rendition="#underline" role="num">7</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell rendition="#float-right">Total</cell>
                            <cell role="num">190</cell>
                        </row>
                    </table></p>
                <pb facs="0385" n="375" xml:id="pg375"/>
                <p>5. The losses of the Allies in submarines during the war are as follows: <table
                        cols="3" rend="width: 70%;" rendition="#center" rows="6">
                        <row role="label">
                            <cell><hi rendition="#italic">Country</hi></cell>
                            <cell><hi rendition="#italic">Number</hi></cell>
                            <cell><hi rendition="#italic">Approximate percentage of each nation’s
                                    submarine losses to total Allied losses in
                                submarines</hi></cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell>Great Britain</cell>
                            <cell role="num">55</cell>
                            <cell role="num">70</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell>France</cell>
                            <cell role="num">14</cell>
                            <cell role="num">18</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell>Italy</cell>
                            <cell role="num">8</cell>
                            <cell role="num">10</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell>U. S. A.</cell>
                            <cell rendition="#underline" role="num">1</cell>
                            <cell rendition="#underline" role="num">2</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell rendition="#float-right">Total</cell>
                            <cell role="num">78</cell>
                            <cell role="num">100</cell>
                        </row>
                    </table></p>
            </div>
